# Migrations

Three independent revision lineages live here, one for each database:

* `channel_*` — channel database (`relay.sqlite`)
* `usage_*` — usage database (`--usage-db`)
* `addrid_*` — address-id database (`--addrid-db`)

Each lineage has its own Alembic version table
(`alembic_version_channel`, `alembic_version_usage`,
`alembic_version_addrid`), because the server keeps the databases separate.

The server runs the appropriate head automatically on startup. Existing
databases created before Alembic used an integer `version` table and the
SQL scripts in `../db-schemas/`; those are upgraded to the initial Alembic
revision and stamped before normal migration runs.

To add a migration, create a revision by hand using the existing naming
scheme (for example `channel_0002_add_something`) and set
`down_revision = "channel_0001"`.
